message: "If you use this repository, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Boltz protein–ligand benchmark: prediction, structural evaluation and training-set similarity analysis"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Trentacoste"
    given-names: "Emilia"
repository-code: "https://github.com/etrentacoste/boltz-protein-ligand-benchmark"
url: "https://github.com/etrentacoste/boltz-protein-ligand-benchmark"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-30
keywords:
  - Boltz-1
  - Boltz-2
  - protein-ligand complex prediction
  - structural bioinformatics
  - ligand RMSD
  - lDDT-PLI
  - PLINDER
  - training-set similarity
  - molecular cofolding
abstract: >
  Code, configurations and processed results used to construct and analyse
  a 100-complex benchmark for protein-ligand structure prediction with
  Boltz-1 and Boltz-2. The repository includes structural evaluation using
  ligand RMSD and lDDT-PLI and PLINDER-based analyses of protein, pocket,
  interaction and ligand similarity to training-set systems.
